model {
  extend basalt.deployment {
    metadata {
      constraint "Pool machine observation credentials are provisioned before their Worker binding. The existing Cloudflare connector executes one reviewed program through its saved OAuth connection; neither the grant nor the new token value leaves that server-side execution. Separate mint and store approvals bind the same program and plan under one writer lease. One account-owned token grants only Workers Containers Read on the exact account, and its value passes directly into the existing default Secrets Store under the stable stage name. The program returns only token ID, secret name and a closed outcome; stored requires an acknowledged value write and is not controller verification. Metadata-only inspection establishes token ownership, never current-value custody after an uncertain rotation. A durable metadata-only submission precedes invocation emission and forbids another create after a lost reply. Recovery requires that original submission and an exact owned-token inspection, then a separately approved rotation or revocation of that token. An uncertain revocation settles from exact absence without repeating DELETE. The bootstrap creates no store, Worker, binding or migration and performs no controller read."
    }
  }
}
